From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ps4-gladius <ps4-gladius@invalid>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 12:10:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: report a fault on a thread that is not Wine's.

A request handler faults while serving GTA IV, and what gets reported is never
that fault. Wine answers a SIGSEGV by raising it as an exception, which walks
segv_handler -> setup_raise_exception -> send_debug_event ->
NtTerminateProcess -> wine_server_call -> server_call_unlocked, and the last
of those reads data->tid. The in-process server runs on a thread the server
creates itself, which has no Wine thread data, so that read is of 0x1c and the
process dies there instead of saying anything.

Each fix so far has only moved where the messenger dies: 0x7c in the debug
buffer, 0x1c in the thread id, 0x1c again in the server call. The fault being
reported has still never been seen.

Print it from the registers before any of that machinery runs. After 0610's
hook, which rewrites these same lines -- placed before it the series stops
applying.

Diagnostic only; the process still dies as it did.

---
diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_x86_64.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_x86_64.c
index 3c4a3e300c..46afb457da 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_x86_64.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_x86_64.c
@@ -2371,6 +2371,23 @@ static void segv_handler( int signal, siginfo_t *siginfo, void *_sigcontext )
 
 #ifdef __PROSPERO__
     if (segv_hook && segv_hook( siginfo, _sigcontext )) return;
+    /* ⚠ DIAGNOSTIC. Everything past this point belongs to a Wine thread: the
+     * fault is raised as an exception, which walks setup_raise_exception,
+     * send_debug_event, NtTerminateProcess and wine_server_call, and the last
+     * of those reads data->tid. The in-process server runs on a thread the
+     * server creates itself, which has no Wine data, so a fault in a request
+     * handler is answered by a second fault inside the machinery reporting the
+     * first -- and the first has never been seen. Say what it was, from the
+     * registers, before any of that runs. */
+    if (!get_thread_data())
+    {
+        extern int sceKernelDebugOutText( int channel, const char *text );
+        char line[176];
+        snprintf( line, sizeof(line),
+                  "wineserver: FAULT on a thread without Wine data: sig %d addr %p rip %p\n",
+                  signal, siginfo ? siginfo->si_addr : NULL, (void *)RIP_sig(sigcontext) );
+        sceKernelDebugOutText( 0, line );
+    }
 #endif
     data = init_handler( sigcontext );
     save_context( data, &context, sigcontext );
